1954,"last":2019,"intercept":0.0,"slope":0.0,"total":0.0},"snow_normal":0.0},"titles":{"year":"2026 so far: 2 daily record highs, no daily record lows","records":"Kahului is setting record highs far faster than chance","change":"Kahului's days and nights both warmed. Days warmed faster.","rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 84\u00b0F was typical for November 13.","t_yest":"November 13: a typical high, but a warm night","p_yest":"The high of <strong>84\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 85\u00b0F, and the record is 92\u00b0F (1968). The low of <strong>72\u00b0F</strong> was the 8th warmest November 13 low (tied) of 73 since 1954.","t_rec":"Kahului is setting record highs far faster than chance","p_rec":"If Kahului's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Kahului has set <strong>99 standing record lows</strong>, fewer than the 135 that chance alone would give, and <strong class=\"sig\">221 record highs</strong>, far more than the 135 that chance alone would give. The 2010s hold the most record highs of any decade (107). Kahului's all-time high is 97\u00b0F, on August 31, 1994.","t_chg":"Kahului's days and nights both warmed. Days warmed faster.","p_chg":"Across 69 complete years: Kahului's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.18\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.06 to +0.30), about +1.2\u00b0F since 1955. Kahului's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.47\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.34 to +0.60), about +3.3\u00b0F since 1955.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 6 of 12 months. Highs rose in all 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Kahului's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.22 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 16.0 inches a year. The wettest year was 1989 (40.63 in); the driest, 2012 (5.04 in). Kahului almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.0 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 2 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}